00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:34.987
Do all for-profit rules apply
in a non-profit setting?"

00:04:35.731 --> 00:04:38.076
- Sam, I love this question, because

00:04:38.076 --> 00:04:39.585
the ironic thing is I think

00:04:39.585 --> 00:04:41.280
the answer is they do map.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.302
I do think that

00:04:42.302 --> 00:04:44.252
if I ever get into, you know, I sit on

00:04:44.252 --> 00:04:46.202
some NGO boards, but if I ever get into

00:04:46.202 --> 00:04:47.642
a chapter of my life where that becomes

00:04:47.642 --> 00:04:49.291
the driving force, I promise you

00:04:49.291 --> 00:04:51.845
my execution in that
world will look exactly

00:04:51.845 --> 00:04:54.050
the same as everything I'm doing here.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:56.047
I do think the rules apply.

00:04:56.047 --> 00:04:57.928
I actually think there's a nuance that

00:04:57.928 --> 00:05:00.575
I want to address which
is that the rules do

00:05:00.575 --> 00:05:04.360
apply, which means an absolute
respect to the customer.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.076
I believe that many people that operate

00:05:07.076 --> 00:05:10.072
in the NGO world have the audacity

00:05:10.072 --> 00:05:12.765
to think there's an
obligation from the wealthy

00:05:12.765 --> 00:05:15.017
or people they know to actually support,

00:05:15.017 --> 00:05:18.778
and that they come across arrogant

00:05:18.778 --> 00:05:21.333
I would say when they're
going in for the ask,

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:22.819
and they're less tactful.

00:05:22.819 --> 00:05:26.371
It's all right hook city in
NGO world, non-profit world,

00:05:26.371 --> 00:05:28.856
and then when somebody
doesn't do something

00:05:28.856 --> 00:05:31.131
they look down on them,
even though the way

00:05:31.131 --> 00:05:33.058
they approach them was completely

00:05:33.058 --> 00:05:34.684
unacceptable in my opinion.

00:05:34.684 --> 00:05:36.495
I do think the rules apply.

00:05:36.495 --> 00:05:38.840
I think you have to bring a value prop.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.046
I think way too many NGOs, non-profits

00:05:41.046 --> 00:05:42.392
mail it in.

00:05:42.392 --> 00:05:44.064
They're not thinking
about that other person's

00:05:44.064 --> 00:05:47.965
life, that person that's
donating life as a whole.

00:05:47.965 --> 00:05:49.405
They're just looking for,

00:05:49.405 --> 00:05:50.891
you know, their tax return,

00:05:50.891 --> 00:05:52.353
and trying to extract dollars,

00:05:52.353 --> 00:05:54.118
and life is about value exchange.

00:05:54.118 --> 00:05:55.604
Even when you're doing good things,

00:05:55.604 --> 00:05:59.407
and that is a huge miss
for so many in this space.

